<title>CANADA: Canada M1 money supply rises in December.</title>
<headline>Canada M1 money supply rises in December.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian M1 money supply rose by C$2.55 billion to C$69.74 billion in December from C$67.19 billion in November and compared with C$61.47 billion in December 1995, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					  Dec 96     Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p>M1					 69.74	67.19	61.47</p>
<p>M2					398.32     397.35     388.64</p>
<p>M3					500.53     498.68     474.12</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Dec	   Nov</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-13.81	-12.67</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     681.94	678.44</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    108.04	109.17</p>
<p>				    Wk to Jan 22  Chg on wk  Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.645  -0.303     +0.724</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     4.082  -3.538     -3.590</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	461.908  -1.219     +4.573</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 131.900  -1.200    -27.300</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  33.408  -0.019     +2.133</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
